WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.849 --> 00:00:05.670
Robb Stark: The ascension of Aegon Targaryen
was confirmed; and the fate of the Seven Kingdoms,

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.640
sealed, on the Field of Fire.

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:13.950
Kings Loren Lannister of the Rock and Mern
Gardener of the Reach stood against Aegon's

00:00:13.950 --> 00:00:15.120
invasion.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:23.950
They commanded a united force of 600 banners,
5,000 mounted knights, and 50,000 men-at-arms.

00:00:23.950 --> 00:00:28.660
Aegon's host was vastly outnumbered, and when
the army of the two kings charged, the invaders

00:00:28.660 --> 00:00:30.640
turned heel and ran.

00:00:30.640 --> 00:00:33.860
But Andal might was no match for dragon flame.

00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:40.269
When Aegon unleashed all three of his dragons,
4,000 souls were horrendously burned alive

00:00:40.269 --> 00:00:43.929
on the battlefield, King Mern among them.

00:00:43.929 --> 00:00:47.809
Realizing all hope was lost, King Loren surrendered.

00:00:47.809 --> 00:00:54.289
The Starks of Winterfell had no intention
of submitting to Targaryen rule.

00:00:54.289 --> 00:00:58.499
They had reigned as Kings in the North since
the days of the First Men, and were determined

00:00:58.499 --> 00:01:03.039
to resist the Targaryen invaders, just as
they had resisted the Andals thousands of

00:01:03.039 --> 00:01:04.659
years before.

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:09.420
King Torrhen Stark led his army to the Red
Fork just east of Riverrun, hoping to succeed

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.570
where Loren and Mern had failed.

00:01:11.570 --> 00:01:18.090
But when Torrhen saw the size of Aegon's now
mighty host along with his monstrous dragons,

00:01:18.090 --> 00:01:23.560
he knew he couldn't subject his followers
to the horror of another field of fire.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.710
He bent the knee and swore fealty to Aegon,
who allowed the Starks to maintain their lordship

00:01:28.710 --> 00:01:33.420
over the region as Lords Paramount and Wardens
of the North.

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:38.969
Without question, Torrhen Stark saved thousands
of lives that day.

00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:43.020
He was ever after known as "the King Who Knelt".

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:48.499
Jaime Lannister: For thousands of years, the
Kingdom of the Rock ruled the Westerlands.

00:01:48.499 --> 00:01:53.030
When the ironborn became a nuisance, my ancestor
sailed to the Iron Islands and returned with

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:58.409
a hundred ironborn hostages, promising to
hang one from the rock every time the ironborn

00:01:58.409 --> 00:02:00.520
dared raid our shores.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:04.409
The ironborn stayed away, well, after twenty
or so.

00:02:04.409 --> 00:02:09.100
When the Andals arrived after sweeping across
the rest of Westeros, we invited their sons

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:12.170
and daughters into the rock as squires and
court ladies.

00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.410
I don't think we ever had to hang any of them.

00:02:16.410 --> 00:02:22.080
Finally, Aegon the Conqueror defeated us on
the Field of Fire, and my ancestor knelt.

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:28.661
Still, little changed but titles and taxes,
for when Visenya Targaryen saw the rock, she

00:02:28.661 --> 00:02:32.450
gave thanks that my ancestor had met Aegon
on the field.

00:02:32.450 --> 00:02:36.420
Even dragon flame would have washed over the
castle like the waves and left just as much

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.420
a mark.

00:02:37.420 --> 00:02:42.040
Randyll Tarly: Most of the Great Houses spout
such nonsense about their origins.

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:48.430
At least my family doesn't claim some long-lost
ancient crown, like the rest of them.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:52.410
House Tarly breeds soldiers, not kings.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:57.390
When House Gardener ruled the Reach, we served
them well and loyally.

00:02:57.390 --> 00:03:04.730
When House Gardener died, and Aegon gave the
Reach to their stewards, House Tyrell, we

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:07.210
served them well and loyally.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:14.230
We know our place, even if the Tyrell women
don't.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:19.800
When Aegon's son faced rebellion from the
Vulture King of Dorne, my ancestor, Savage

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:24.650
Sam Tarly, led the royal forces on a Vulture
Hunt.

00:03:24.650 --> 00:03:31.770
Heartsbane, our ancestral Valyrian sword,
and the pride of our House, soon ran red from

00:03:31.770 --> 00:03:34.030
point to hilt with rebel blood.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:40.370
Brynden Tully: Men have fought over the Riverlands
since the Dawn Age, but that's to be expected

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:42.900
of things that rest below the Neck.

00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:47.180
Doesn't help that the Riverlands are between
everything and everything else.

00:03:47.180 --> 00:03:55.200
The Westerlands' gold, the Reach's grain,
the Vale's rock, and the North's... snow?

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.590
House Mudd once ruled as the Kings of the
Rivers and Hills, but after a thousand years,

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:07.010
their line was exhausted and fell to the Storm
Kings, who fell to the ironborn.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:12.450
I suppose after years of drowning at sea,
our rivers looked pretty attractive to that

00:04:12.450 --> 00:04:14.350
race of pirates.

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:21.180
Never mind that their monstrous castle, Harrenhal,
was too large to staff and garrison.

00:04:21.180 --> 00:04:25.190
It turned out the ironborn would not be there
long enough to bother.

00:04:25.190 --> 00:04:31.630
Aegon Targaryen landed to our south and, as
had many before him, liked the look of the

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:32.840
Riverlands.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:37.510
My ancestor Edmyn Tully led the desertion
of Riverlords to his cause and was rewarded

00:04:37.510 --> 00:04:41.250
by getting to watch King Harren burn in his
own tower.

00:04:41.250 --> 00:04:46.070
Unfortunately, that's not all Edmyn got.

00:04:46.070 --> 00:04:51.930
House Tully was named the Lord Paramount of
the Trident, which means we had to keep in

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:57.910
line all those lords who hadn't governed themselves
for thousands of years.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:03.590
Yet under the Targaryens, the Riverlands knew
a peace we hadn't had for centuries, if ever.

00:05:03.590 --> 00:05:05.250
But like all good things, sooner or later,
it all goes to shit.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:08.870
Theon Greyjoy: When Aegon and his dragons
burned Harren the Black and all his sons at

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:13.470
Harrenhal, the days when men feared the sight
of our longships were over.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:16.350
Aegon would not permit marauders and raiders
in his Seven Kingdoms.

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:20.770
With Harren died our empire and the Old Way
that forged it.

00:05:20.770 --> 00:05:23.330
But what is dead may never die.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:25.910
Petyr Baelish: Impregnable.

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:28.639
That's how the Vale sees itself.

00:05:28.639 --> 00:05:31.050
Shielded from Westeros by its mountains.

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:34.030
Except the Vale has been conquered.

00:05:34.030 --> 00:05:38.639
Those vaunted mountains didn't stop the Andals
who came by the eastern sea.

00:05:38.639 --> 00:05:42.900
The people of the Vale say that Ser Artys
Arryn, the Andal general, flew on the back

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:48.460
of a giant falcon and slew the Griffin King
on top of the tallest mountain.

00:05:48.460 --> 00:05:54.139
During Aegon's conquest, one of his sisters
did the same, flying a dragon over the Bloody

00:05:54.139 --> 00:05:56.980
Gate and up to the Eyrie, the Arryn stronghold.

00:05:56.980 --> 00:06:02.330
And the Arryn boy-king yielded the Vale in
return for a ride on the beast.

00:06:02.330 --> 00:06:05.430
Do you sense the theme here?

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:10.151
The rationalizing of defeats with mythical
beasts and the whims of children, instead

00:06:10.151 --> 00:06:14.650
of acknowledging the root cause – the arrogance
of isolation.

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:21.320
Brienne of Tarth: The first Storm King, Durran,
started his reign by declaring war on the

00:06:21.320 --> 00:06:23.340
gods themselves.

00:06:23.340 --> 00:06:27.740
He loved the daughter of the sea god and the
wind goddess, but they forbade the union.

00:06:27.740 --> 00:06:32.710
At their wedding, the gods unleashed their
might, pulling down his hold and killing all

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:36.480
of Durran's family and guests, though his
wife shielded him.

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:43.710
Durran vowed to rebuild, and when he did,
the gods again destroyed his home.

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:48.940
His councilors begged him to retreat inland,
but he would not abandon his war.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:53.120
Finally, with the council of the Children
of the Forest, or perhaps a young Bran the

00:06:53.120 --> 00:06:59.470
Builder, Durran raised a seventh castle that,
try as they might and still do, the wind and

00:06:59.470 --> 00:07:01.830
sea gods could not tear asunder.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:08.600
Durran took the name Godsgrief and called
his new home Storm's End.

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:13.480
Having beaten the waters to the east, the
Storm Kings turned their gaze to more practical

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:17.669
enemies, the Reach, the Riverlands, and Dorne.

00:07:17.669 --> 00:07:21.699
For thousands of years, the Storm Kings fought
the Gardener Kings of the Reach and various

00:07:21.699 --> 00:07:27.669
families of Dorne for control of the Dornish
Marches, just below the Red Mountains.

00:07:27.669 --> 00:07:32.440
The fighting did not stop until Dorne married
into the Seven Kingdoms, a mere hundred years

00:07:32.440 --> 00:07:33.440
ago.

00:07:33.440 --> 00:07:38.691
But still, the houses of the Stormlands, such
as the Dondarrions, guard the Boneway, the

00:07:38.691 --> 00:07:43.440
mountain pass into the Marches, against any
Dornish incursion.

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.850
The Storm Kings had greater luck to their
north at first.

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:52.090
They took the Trident from the River Kings
and built an empire that stretched as far

00:07:52.090 --> 00:07:53.790
as the Neck.

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:58.199
But then the ironborn swarmed out of their
islands and pushed the Storm Kings out of

00:07:58.199 --> 00:07:59.199
the Riverlands.

00:07:59.199 --> 00:08:04.889
No doubt, the ironborn intended to expand
their empire into the Stormlands.

00:08:04.889 --> 00:08:09.260
Before they had a chance, Aegon Targaryen
landed with his dragons.

00:08:09.260 --> 00:08:16.199
While Aegon burned the kings of the Iron Islands,
the Rock and the Reach, his fiercest commander

00:08:16.199 --> 00:08:21.040
and rumored bastard brother, Orys Baratheon,
set out to subdue the Stormlands.

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:27.070
No matter how fierce a warrior he was, no
one could have envied his task.

00:08:27.070 --> 00:08:32.550
Storm's End had seen thousands of years of
war and never fallen, but Argilac, the Storm

00:08:32.550 --> 00:08:37.550
King, chose not to barricade himself behind
its walls and gave Orys the battle he must

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:39.079
have hoped for.

00:08:39.079 --> 00:08:48.300
Orys slew Argilac and took Argilac's castle,
kingdom, daughter, sigil, and House words.

00:08:48.300 --> 00:08:50.890
House Baratheon became the Lord of the Stormlands.

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:56.440
Viserys Targaryen: The Targaryen dynasty united
the Seven Kingdoms and lasted nearly three

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:58.269
centuries.

00:08:58.269 --> 00:09:04.060
It was a dynasty forged in fire, sealed in
blood, and destroyed by rebellion.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:11.240
The Targaryens are blood of the dragon, descended
from the nobility of ancient Valyria, a once-mighty

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:13.240
empire in the east.

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:19.220
When the cataclysmic Doom laid waste of Valyria
and its people, the Targaryens survived, having

00:09:19.220 --> 00:09:22.579
settled in the island fortress of Dragonstone
years before.

00:09:22.579 --> 00:09:28.540
They remained there for a century until the
rise of Aegon the Conqueror.

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:35.319
Instead of attempting to reclaim the eastern
lands of his ancestors, Aegon sailed west

00:09:35.319 --> 00:09:41.730
for the Seven Kingdoms, his sisters Visenya
and Rhaenys at his side.

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:47.089
To keep the bloodlines pure, Aegon continued
the custom of his Valyrian ancestors and took

00:09:47.089 --> 00:09:49.689
both of his sisters to wives.

00:09:49.689 --> 00:09:53.970
Together, they came ashore on the eastern
coast of Westeros.

00:09:53.970 --> 00:10:00.189
Their blazon: a dragon with three heads, representing
Aegon and his sister-wives.

00:10:00.189 --> 00:10:05.370
Their words: "Fire and Blood."

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:11.160
While their host was small when compared to
the armies of the Seven Kingdoms, Aegon and

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:12.699
his sisters had a secret weapon.

00:10:12.699 --> 00:10:17.339
The last of the dragons.

00:10:17.339 --> 00:10:22.709
He conquered every kingdom, save Dorne, which
eventually bowed to Targaryen rule a century

00:10:22.709 --> 00:10:23.709
later.

00:10:23.709 --> 00:10:29.040
He had the swords of his enemies melted down
by the fiery breath of his dragon, Balerion

00:10:29.040 --> 00:10:33.529
the Black Dread, and forged into the Iron
Throne.

00:10:33.529 --> 00:10:39.380
The capital city of King's Landing was built
on the eastern coast, where Aegon and his

00:10:39.380 --> 00:10:40.910
sisters first came ashore.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:47.170
And Aegon ordered the construction of a royal
castle on its highest hill, the Red Keep.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:53.779
For three hundred years the Targaryen dynasty
stood strong, in the face of rebellion, civil

00:10:53.779 --> 00:10:54.610
war, and plague.

